PART B — THEORY TO WRITE ON PAPER

BACKGROUND / THEORY (50–100 WORDS)

Website crawling involves discovering webpages, links and website structure. OSINT investigators use URL discovery to locate relevant pages and understand how information is organised. Search interfaces can find relevant webpages, while archive services can show historical snapshots when available. Dedicated crawlers systematically follow website links and list internal URLs. Search results alone do not guarantee a complete internal-link inventory, so the tool must match the practical objective.


OPEN-SOURCE TOOL (AROUND 50 WORDS)

WebCrawler is a search interface that helps discover relevant webpages and URLs. The Internet Archive's Wayback Machine provides archived snapshots of websites when available. For systematic internal-link crawling, Screaming Frog SEO Spider can discover URLs and display website structure. The appropriate tool depends on whether the task is finding related pages, checking historical versions or mapping internal links.


PERFORMANCE STEPS

1. Search the Prakash Raj–Chandrayaan-3 case in WebCrawler.

